# People finder

A household rarely needs a public people directory, so list roles, not individuals. Where an installation has users or responsible contacts, account permissions stay in Home Assistant’s own account settings. For example, show “Heating maintainer” rather than a name, email address or whether they are home. Scope, result count, empty states, focus and the no-JavaScript fallback follow the [shared finder behaviour](../finder.html#finder-shared-contract).

## When to use it

Use it for role examples only. Where a private installation includes users or responsible contacts, use Home Assistant’s account and permission management.

## Home Assistant boundary

Do not copy a government office hierarchy. Do not expose presence, location, email addresses or account permissions in a public finder.

